---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CtaBanner from '../components/CtaBanner.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Why We Don't Partner | Clinic Data Sovereignty Manifesto | LamaniSync"
  description="Read why LamaniSync doesn't wait for legacy CMS vendor permission, pay partner taxes, or allow software cartels to hold your clinic's calendar hostage. The Dropbox Analogy and clinic data rights."
>
  <!-- Manifesto Hero -->
  <section class="manifesto-hero">
    <div class="bg-grid-pattern"></div>
    <div class="hero-glow"></div>
    <div class="container hero-content">
      <div class="attio-badge crimson">
        <svg style="width:12px; height:12px;" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="4.93" y1="4.93" x2="19.07" y2="19.07"/></svg>
        <span>A Manifesto on Healthcare Data Sovereignty</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="hero-title">
        <span class="heading-dark">Why We Don't Partner</span><br />
        <span class="heading-muted">With Legacy CMS Vendors.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">
        We built LamaniSync because clinics deserve modern AI booking, sub-second WhatsApp scheduling, and total freedom over their own calendar data—without waiting 12 months for vendor approval or paying extortionate "partner taxes."
      </p>

      <div class="manifesto-author-pill">
        <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1534528741775-53994a69daeb?w=100&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80" alt="Author" class="author-img" />
        <div class="author-info">
          <span class="author-name">The LamaniSync Founding Team</span>
          <span class="author-meta">Published for independent clinics & healthcare practitioners</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Core Thesis / Callout Section -->
  <section class="section thesis-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="thesis-card">
        <div class="quote-mark">“</div>
        <p class="thesis-statement">
          When you install Dropbox or Google Drive on your computer, you do not call Microsoft or Apple to ask for permission. You bought the computer. You own the files. <strong>The software on your front desk should serve your clinic, not the other way around.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 1: The Walled Garden Problem -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head text-center">
        <div class="attio-badge crimson">
          <span>Problem Statement</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="section-title">
          <span class="heading-dark">The Walled Garden Problem</span><br />
          <span class="heading-muted">How legacy healthcare vendors stifle innovation.</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Legacy Clinic Management Systems (CMS / EHR) have maintained an artificial monopoly over medical practices for decades through three predatory practices.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tactic-grid">
        <div class="tactic-card">
          <div class="tactic-num">01</div>
          <h3 class="tactic-title">The Extortionate "Partner Tax"</h3>
          <p class="tactic-text">
            Legacy vendors charge third-party innovators between $10,000 to $25,000 in upfront "certification fees", plus recurring monthly revenue shares. These costs are ultimately passed directly to your clinic in bloated monthly invoices.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tactic-card">
          <div class="tactic-num">02</div>
          <h3 class="tactic-title">The 12-Month Red Tape Queue</h3>
          <p class="tactic-text">
            When you request an integration for a modern tool like Sara AI WhatsApp bookings, vendors intentionally drag paperwork out for 6 to 12 months. Their goal is simple: wear you down until you give up and settle for their own inferior add-on.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tactic-card">
          <div class="tactic-num">03</div>
          <h3 class="tactic-title">Artificial API Throttling</h3>
          <p class="tactic-text">
            Even when vendors offer official APIs, they frequently throttle sync to once every 4 hours or disable real-time slot checking. They do this deliberately so outside tools cannot provide instant 24/7 patient booking.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: The Dropbox Analogy -->
  <section class="section bg-light">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="analogy-box">
        <div class="analogy-badge">The Technical Analogy</div>
        <h2 class="analogy-title">
          <span class="heading-dark">The Dropbox Analogy</span><br />
          <span class="heading-muted">Why your workstation is your sovereign domain.</span>
        </h2>
        
        <div class="analogy-content">
          <p>
            Consider how cloud storage revolutionised personal computing in 2008. When Dropbox launched, they didn't wait for Windows or macOS to grant them an "exclusive partner license." 
          </p>
          <p>
            Instead, Dropbox built a desktop client that simply watched the folder on your hard drive. As the owner of the machine, <strong>you</strong> gave Dropbox permission to sync your files. Microsoft didn't get a veto, and Apple didn't get to block your access.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>The web browser is the modern operating system of your clinic.</strong> 
          </p>
          <p>
            Your front-desk computer belongs to your healthcare practice. Your receptionists log in using legitimate clinic credentials. When LamaniSync runs as a Chrome Extension inside that browser tab, it is acting as your clinic's authorized digital assistant. 
          </p>
          <p class="analogy-highlight">
            You do not need permission from your CMS vendor to read your own clinic's calendar, just like you do not need permission from Dell or HP to open a document on your screen.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3: Vendor FUD Debunked -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head text-center">
        <div class="attio-badge crimson">
          <span>Myth Busting</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="section-title">
          <span class="heading-dark">Debunking Vendor FUD</span><br />
          <span class="heading-muted">Fear, Uncertainty, and Doubt vs Engineering Reality.</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          When legacy vendors lose their monopoly over your clinic, they deploy aggressive scare tactics. Here is the technical and legal reality.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="fud-grid">
        <!-- Row 1 -->
        <div class="fud-card">
          <div class="fud-myth">
            <span class="fud-label myth">Vendor FUD</span>
            <h4>"This integration is unauthorized and violates our policy!"</h4>
            <p>Vendors send scary letters claiming that connecting third-party tools violates their terms.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="fud-arrow">→</div>
          <div class="fud-reality">
            <span class="fud-label reality">Legal Reality</span>
            <h4>"Unauthorized" simply means without paying vendor tax</h4>
            <p>Under the <strong>Malaysian PDPA</strong> and the US <strong>21st Century Cures Act</strong>, blocking a healthcare provider from accessing or porting their own patient appointment data is illegal <em>information blocking</em>. You are the legal data custodian.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 2 -->
        <div class="fud-card">
          <div class="fud-myth">
            <span class="fud-label myth">Vendor FUD</span>
            <h4>"It poses a massive security breach and data leak risk!"</h4>
            <p>Vendors imply that browser extensions expose patient records to the open internet.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="fud-arrow">→</div>
          <div class="fud-reality">
            <span class="fud-label reality">Engineering Reality</span>
            <h4>Far more secure than legacy on-premise Windows agents</h4>
            <p>LamaniSync operates inside Chrome's Manifest V3 sandbox with <strong>zero open inbound ports</strong>, hardware-backed <strong>WebCrypto Ed25519 device signatures</strong>, and exact-origin scoping. It never stores raw PHI in local storage.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Row 3 -->
        <div class="fud-card">
          <div class="fud-myth">
            <span class="fud-label myth">Vendor FUD</span>
            <h4>"Writing data directly will corrupt the clinic database!"</h4>
            <p>Vendors warn that appointments inserted without their blessing will break calendar tables.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="fud-arrow">→</div>
          <div class="fud-reality">
            <span class="fud-label reality">Engineering Reality</span>
            <h4>Zero direct database injection; 100% readback verified</h4>
            <p>LamaniSync never touches raw SQL tables. It writes exclusively through the CMS's own front-end application layer with native validation, followed by <strong>cryptographic read-after-write verification</strong>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4: The 4 Pillars of Clinic Data Sovereignty -->
  <section class="section bg-light">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head text-center">
        <div class="attio-badge blue">
          <span>Our Guiding Principles</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="section-title">
          <span class="heading-dark">The 4 Pillars</span>
          <span class="heading-muted">of Clinic Data Sovereignty.</span>
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="pillars-container">
        <div class="p-card">
          <div class="p-num">01</div>
          <h3>Clinics Own the Data, Not Software Vendors</h3>
          <p>The patient records, operatory calendars, and doctor schedules belong to your healthcare practice and the patients you serve. Software vendors are mere electronic custodians.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-card">
          <div class="p-num">02</div>
          <h3>The Workstation is Sovereign</h3>
          <p>Any software you authorize to run in your clinic's browser on your hardware is your decision. You do not need third-party approval to orchestrate your own workflows.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-card">
          <div class="p-num">03</div>
          <h3>Zero-Trust Sandboxing Over Vendor Secrecy</h3>
          <p>Security is achieved through verifiable cryptography, exact-origin sandboxing, and ephemeral memory execution—not through vendor lock-in disguised as "compliance."</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-card">
          <div class="p-num">04</div>
          <h3>100% Readback-Verified Writes</h3>
          <p>We hold our software to clinical-grade reliability standards: an appointment is never promised to a patient until verified directly from the primary calendar store.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA Banner -->
  <CtaBanner />
</Layout>

<style>
  .manifesto-hero {
    position: relative;
    padding: 5.5rem 0 3.5rem 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .hero-glow {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: min(700px, 100%);
    max-width: 100%;
    height: 380px;
    background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.025) 0%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 70%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .hero-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .hero-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4.5vw, 3.8rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 900px;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .hero-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 760px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .manifesto-author-pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    background: #f8fafc;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-hairline);
    padding: 0.45rem 1rem 0.45rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    max-width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .author-img {
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .author-info {
    text-align: left;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .author-name {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #0a0a0a;
  }

  .author-meta {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    word-break: break-word;
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .manifesto-author-pill {
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    }
    .author-meta {
      font-size: 0.68rem;
    }
  }

  /* Thesis Callout */
  .thesis-section {
    padding: 2rem 0;
  }

  .thesis-card {
    background: #0f172a;
    border: 1px solid #1e293b;
    color: #ffffff;
    border-radius: var(--radius-container);
    padding: 3.5rem 3rem;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
  }

  .quote-mark {
    position: absolute;
    top: -20px;
    left: 20px;
    font-size: 10rem;
    font-family: serif;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    line-height: 1;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .thesis-statement {
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.2vw, 1.65rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.5;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 950px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    text-align: center;
    color: #f1f5f9;
  }

  .thesis-statement strong {
    color: #ffffff;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* Tactics Grid */
  .section {
    padding: 5rem 0;
  }

  .section.bg-light {
    background: #fafafa;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-hairline);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .section-head.text-center {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .section-head .attio-badge {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .section-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.2vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .section-desc {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 680px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .tactic-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .tactic-card {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    padding: 2.25rem 2rem;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.02);
    transition: transform 0.2s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), box-shadow 0.2s;
  }

  .tactic-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: #cbd5e1;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
  }

  .tactic-num {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--primary);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .tactic-title {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .tactic-text {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Analogy Box */
  .analogy-box {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-container);
    padding: 3.5rem 3rem;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.03);
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .analogy-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: #fff1f3;
    color: var(--primary);
    border: 1px solid #fecdd6;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .analogy-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .analogy-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: #334155;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .analogy-highlight {
    background: #f8fafc;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--primary);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  /* FUD Grid */
  .fud-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    max-width: 1050px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .fud-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1.2fr;
    align-items: center;
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    padding: 2rem;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.02);
  }

  .fud-label {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
  }

  .fud-label.myth {
    background: #fef2f2;
    color: #991b1b;
    border-color: #fee2e2;
  }

  .fud-label.reality {
    background: #f0fdf4;
    color: #166534;
    border-color: #dcfce7;
  }

  .fud-myth h4 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .fud-myth p {
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .fud-arrow {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #94a3b8;
  }

  .fud-reality h4 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .fud-reality p {
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: #334155;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* Pillars */
  .pillars-container {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .p-card {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    padding: 2.25rem 2rem;
    box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.02);
    transition: transform 0.2s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), box-shadow 0.2s;
  }

  .p-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: #cbd5e1;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
  }

  .p-num {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--primary);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .p-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }

  .p-card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .tactic-grid,
    .pillars-container {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .fud-card {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }
    .fud-arrow {
      display: none;
    }
    .thesis-card,
    .analogy-box {
      padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .manifesto-hero {
      padding: 4rem 0 2.5rem 0;
    }
    .fud-card {
      padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
    }
    .analogy-box,
    .thesis-card {
      padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
    }
    .tactic-card,
    .p-card {
      padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
    }
    .section {
      padding: 3.5rem 0;
    }
  }
</style>
